<title>INDIA: India sees 96/97 sugar cane output at 267.5 mln T.</title>
<headline>India sees 96/97 sugar cane output at 267.5 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's sugar cane output in 1996/97 (Oct-Sept) is expected to fall to 267.5 million tonnes from 282.9 million in 1995/96, Food and Agriculture Minister Chaturanan Mishra said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Mishra told parliament the anticipated fall in cane production was due to a fall in the area devoted to the crop because of prolonged crushing in the last season.</p>
<p>&quot;This meant that land was not released for cultivation in the subsequent year,&quot; Mishra said.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
